1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:07,000
Threatened by a ruthless demon, humanity was on the brink of destruction.

2
00:00:11,000 --> 00:00:16,000
All seemed lost until a lone mage stepped forward and took up the fight.

3
00:00:22,000 --> 00:00:28,000
After his triumph, he was hailed as the Wizard King, and his story became legend.

4
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:34,000
Check that out! It's a floating castle!

5
00:00:34,000 --> 00:00:38,000
This is it. We're at the Eye of the Midnight Sun's hideout.

6
00:00:40,000 --> 00:00:47,000
The Royal Knights, an elite team of fighters chosen to defeat the Eye of the Midnight Sun, were finally putting their plan into action.

7
00:00:49,000 --> 00:00:51,000
Yeah, that's lit. No doubt about it.

8
00:00:51,000 --> 00:00:54,000
So we'll divide into five teams of four and make our move.

9
00:00:54,000 --> 00:00:57,000
Team one will charge in from the upper left!

10
00:00:57,000 --> 00:00:58,000
Yes, ma'am.

11
00:00:58,000 --> 00:01:00,000
Team two, take the lower left!

12
00:01:00,000 --> 00:01:01,000
Yes, ma'am!

13
00:01:01,000 --> 00:01:03,000
Team three, cover the upper right!

14
00:01:03,000 --> 00:01:04,000
Yes, ma'am!

15
00:01:04,000 --> 00:01:06,000
Team four, take the lower right!

16
00:01:06,000 --> 00:01:07,000
Yes, ma'am!

17
00:01:07,000 --> 00:01:10,000
And we three members of team five will attack them head on!

18
00:01:10,000 --> 00:01:11,000
Ma'am!

19
00:01:11,000 --> 00:01:17,000
All that matters is whether you're strong or weak. And the two of you are here because you're strong, isn't that correct?

20
00:01:17,000 --> 00:01:18,000
Yeah.

21
00:01:18,000 --> 00:01:20,000
Two fools chosen by Yami.

22
00:01:20,000 --> 00:01:23,000
I hope for your sakes you do not disappoint me.

23
00:01:23,000 --> 00:01:24,000
Yes, ma'am!

24
00:01:24,000 --> 00:01:29,000
Yeah, we'll do our best to come back in one piece. Is that good enough for you?

25
00:01:29,000 --> 00:01:36,000
A team like you shouldn't need a fully detailed battle plan. Eliminate any who dare to get in your way as you head toward the center.

26
00:01:36,000 --> 00:01:41,000
And of course, the method is up to you!

27
00:01:41,000 --> 00:01:49,000
Once they arrived in the strong magic region known as Gravitostones, the heroes invaded the floating dungeon that served as the enemy's hideout and headed for the center.

28
00:01:49,000 --> 00:01:54,000
Their ultimate goal was to eliminate Litt, the terrorist organization's elusive leader.

29
00:01:54,000 --> 00:01:59,000
Whoa! Crazy! I feel like she doesn't even need our help!

30
00:02:01,000 --> 00:02:05,000
Meanwhile, at the Black Bull's hideout, the mood was more relaxed.

31
00:02:21,000 --> 00:02:23,000
Well, I guess I'm heading out.

32
00:02:23,000 --> 00:02:24,000
What's going on, Captain?

33
00:02:24,000 --> 00:02:28,000
I just got this letter from Goldie Guts asking to speak with me.

34
00:02:28,000 --> 00:02:31,000
Sounds like he wants to apologize for the longest thing.

35
00:02:32,000 --> 00:02:37,000
So I'm off to their HQ. Although, I'm not sure why I'm the one that has to go where he is.

36
00:02:37,000 --> 00:02:40,000
Seems like the apologizer should have to make the trip.

37
00:02:40,000 --> 00:02:43,000
Does this mean I can go and visit Marie while you're away?

38
00:02:43,000 --> 00:02:47,000
I can't believe you just asked me that. You stay put in case a mission comes in.

39
00:02:48,000 --> 00:02:52,000
I wanted to go check on Finral, so I'll be out for a bit, too.

40
00:02:52,000 --> 00:02:57,000
How long can that boy stay asleep? Maybe if he senses I'm there, he'll wake up.

41
00:02:57,000 --> 00:02:59,000
And I've got some training to do.

42
00:03:00,000 --> 00:03:03,000
I'm gonna get crazy strong. You wait and see.

43
00:03:04,000 --> 00:03:09,000
Good luck, Magna. I know you didn't get into the Royal Knights, but try not to let it get you down, you little troublemaker.

44
00:03:09,000 --> 00:03:12,000
I know. There's an insult in there somewhere. I just can't tell where.

45
00:03:12,000 --> 00:03:17,000
I'm going out to hunt for delicious goodies! I'll dig up a smorgasbord!

46
00:03:18,000 --> 00:03:20,000
Come back soon, okay, you guys?

47
00:03:20,000 --> 00:03:31,000
All right, I'll be back in a while. Do me a favor and don't let the place get overrun by robbers while I'm gone.

48
00:03:31,000 --> 00:03:38,000
Oh, boy. This is gonna be a drag.

49
00:03:39,000 --> 00:03:43,000
Well, when you see that old quack, ask him how Finral's holding up.

50
00:03:43,000 --> 00:03:46,000
You got it, Captain Yami.

51
00:03:47,000 --> 00:03:49,000
Here goes. Training time!

52
00:03:53,000 --> 00:03:58,000
Hope you're ready, my scrumptious little sweets. The moment I've been growing you for is finally here!

53
00:03:59,000 --> 00:04:04,000
Charmy and the She-Cooks are on the way to harvest every last one of you for snogging!

54
00:04:05,000 --> 00:04:16,000
� 義兄 聞 聞 キミのこと

55
00:04:17,000 --> 00:04:21,000
ワ ワ ワ わかんないこれはわからないだから

56
00:04:22,000 --> 00:04:23,740
ぼ わ ��モ

57
00:04:24,800 --> 00:04:26,040
ボ  disciple

58
00:04:34,000 --> 00:05:03,980
Thank you.

59
00:05:04,000 --> 00:05:33,980
Thank you.

60
00:05:34,000 --> 00:06:03,980
Thank you.

61
00:06:04,000 --> 00:06:07,460
Hey!

62
00:06:07,760 --> 00:06:08,460
I'm sorry!

63
00:06:13,440 --> 00:06:16,460
If a mission request comes our way, I'll handle it myself.

64
00:06:16,960 --> 00:06:19,360
You two feel free to go to your rooms and get some rest.

65
00:06:20,000 --> 00:06:23,460
Oh no! Please don't jump on yourself on my account! I would rather die!

66
00:06:23,460 --> 00:06:33,640
I can't understand a word they're saying. Just take some time to relax.

67
00:06:33,920 --> 00:06:38,600
Besides, I need all the work I can get so I'll have extra money to pay tribute to my darling sister.

68
00:06:38,600 --> 00:06:50,120
I'm too shy to go without transformation magic and let people see my true self anyway!

69
00:06:50,120 --> 00:07:01,580
Then again, all the other black bulls do think of me as a friend, and if that's the case, then I should at least be myself in front of them, right?

70
00:07:01,580 --> 00:07:08,820
Besides, don't she even complimented this version of me!

71
00:07:11,040 --> 00:07:16,140
All right, that's enough!

72
00:07:16,140 --> 00:07:22,400
I'm going to my room so I can concentrate on making a doll of my sweet goddess. Let me know if anything happens.

73
00:07:22,400 --> 00:07:31,360
It's bad enough to be in a group of three, but if you leave us alone, it'll be a one-on-one and everyone knows it's the most uncomfortable thing of all!

74
00:07:31,600 --> 00:07:34,820
I mean, Gordon's pretty quiet too, but it doesn't really even matter who it is!

75
00:07:35,000 --> 00:07:38,660
If I have to be alone with another person, I'm going to melt into a funnel of humiliation!

76
00:07:40,200 --> 00:07:42,240
What is the matter with these two?

77
00:07:42,900 --> 00:07:46,120
Muster up your courage! Try to make some casual conversation!

78
00:07:46,120 --> 00:07:52,360
Hey, G-G-Gosh, that's an interesting project you're working on there! What exactly is it?

79
00:07:52,740 --> 00:07:53,440
Oh, this?

80
00:07:54,260 --> 00:07:54,860
Uh, yeah!

81
00:07:55,240 --> 00:08:02,340
I'm glad you asked. You see, when I was a nerd, my eyes were open to the wonder of figurines, so I'm making one depicting Marie in one-eighth scale.

82
00:08:03,180 --> 00:08:04,760
Wow, that's, uh...

83
00:08:04,760 --> 00:08:08,500
I'll let you worship her once I finish it.

84
00:08:09,160 --> 00:08:11,300
Um, should I be grateful? Sorry!

85
00:08:16,120 --> 00:08:18,040
I'll let you worship my own culture.

86
00:08:18,520 --> 00:08:20,700
Oh no, please don't! I'd rather not see that!

87
00:08:21,140 --> 00:08:22,280
Uh, pink!

88
00:08:24,520 --> 00:08:25,060
Ah!

89
00:08:27,060 --> 00:08:29,440
I'm sorry, I'm sorry, I'm sorry.

90
00:08:30,300 --> 00:08:31,080
I'm sorry.

91
00:08:32,220 --> 00:08:35,500
This has been his cloaks been full of voodoo dolls his entire time!

92
00:08:37,000 --> 00:08:39,220
Ew, I don't like this at all!

93
00:08:39,800 --> 00:08:42,400
Do you have any clue how scary you are?

94
00:08:42,400 --> 00:08:49,100
I know I've got no room to talk, but if building friendships is that important to you, that means you have to be more approachable.

95
00:08:49,560 --> 00:08:51,120
And you can start with your face.

96
00:08:52,980 --> 00:08:55,000
Try smiling for once.

97
00:08:56,380 --> 00:08:57,200
Go on.

98
00:08:59,800 --> 00:09:00,900
That's even worse!

99
00:09:00,900 --> 00:09:09,840
Well, anyway, nature's calling.

100
00:09:11,700 --> 00:09:12,740
Don't touch her!

101
00:09:12,960 --> 00:09:13,600
I got it!

102
00:09:15,280 --> 00:09:16,900
Oh, wait, where is it?

103
00:09:17,900 --> 00:09:20,440
It's on the second floor today, down the hall for the night.

104
00:09:21,180 --> 00:09:21,500
Gotcha.

105
00:09:21,860 --> 00:09:25,300
I still don't understand why this building has to change its layout all the time.

106
00:09:25,380 --> 00:09:27,100
It's really annoying to keep track of.

107
00:09:27,420 --> 00:09:27,820
I'm not sure.

108
00:09:28,180 --> 00:09:29,680
It's been a long time to be long.

109
00:09:29,680 --> 00:09:31,680
Ugh, what a headache.

110
00:09:32,240 --> 00:09:35,060
I'm sure it's some kind of spell, but what's the point of having it?

111
00:09:35,480 --> 00:09:37,780
Please come back as quickly as you can, okay, Ghosh?

112
00:09:37,880 --> 00:09:40,400
Like I said before, I'm extremely uncomfortable with this.

113
00:09:40,540 --> 00:09:42,840
What were Charmy and Vanessa gossiping about earlier?

114
00:09:43,980 --> 00:09:45,400
I saw something creepy!

115
00:09:45,880 --> 00:09:49,840
It was hard to make out, but it was definitely fluffy, and it wasn't a sheep cookie either!

116
00:09:49,840 --> 00:09:52,220
It was way more spooky and mysterious than that!

117
00:09:53,000 --> 00:09:55,640
I swear it's not the alcohol talking.

118
00:09:56,080 --> 00:09:57,360
I'm telling the truth.

119
00:09:57,420 --> 00:09:58,460
I saw a ghost.

120
00:09:58,620 --> 00:09:59,840
A real-life ghost.

121
00:10:01,300 --> 00:10:02,260
I'm serious!

122
00:10:03,120 --> 00:10:05,680
What if it's not a spell and our hideout really is haunted?

123
00:10:05,680 --> 00:10:07,520
Come on!

124
00:10:07,520 --> 00:10:10,360
You know it's not funny to joke around about things like that!

125
00:10:10,360 --> 00:10:26,800
We're surrounded!

126
00:10:26,800 --> 00:10:37,100
Oh no, this is evil! Please try not to look at me! It's too humiliating!

127
00:10:37,460 --> 00:10:41,460
We have bigger problems here! Hurry up and transform already!

128
00:10:44,980 --> 00:10:50,040
No, you idiot! I don't know what's going on, but these people are the opposite of our friends!

129
00:10:50,800 --> 00:10:51,840
Get ready for battle!

130
00:10:56,800 --> 00:10:59,980
What do you think they're doing?

131
00:11:01,580 --> 00:11:04,060
So this place is Asta's hideout.

132
00:11:04,940 --> 00:11:07,440
But I guess Asta isn't around today, huh?

133
00:11:08,240 --> 00:11:11,600
That's too bad. I was looking forward to dissecting him alive.

134
00:11:12,100 --> 00:11:16,400
Sally, for the last time he isn't your play theme because he belongs to me.

135
00:11:16,820 --> 00:11:19,660
I was excited to have some fun with him today, too.

136
00:11:20,140 --> 00:11:24,960
Sally, Radies, look. You do well to remember our current objective.

137
00:11:24,960 --> 00:11:32,940
Huh. I guess if this is the Black Bull's secret hideout, I'll probably find plenty of toys just begging to be mine.

138
00:11:33,220 --> 00:11:34,560
I can't wait for it.

139
00:11:34,640 --> 00:11:39,660
Yay, experiments! I want to cut them open! Rearrange their innards!

140
00:11:39,840 --> 00:11:41,340
Watch them bleed out!

141
00:11:41,340 --> 00:11:56,060
All right, intruders, listen up.

142
00:11:56,320 --> 00:11:59,560
I don't know whose stupid decision it was to break in here like this.

143
00:11:59,980 --> 00:12:00,400
Phew.

144
00:12:01,400 --> 00:12:02,900
But you will pay!

145
00:12:02,900 --> 00:12:15,300
Ah, here they are. Those rotten magic knights.

146
00:12:16,200 --> 00:12:17,420
You guys again?

147
00:12:20,920 --> 00:12:22,460
Of course I know them.

148
00:12:23,180 --> 00:12:26,080
They're all terrorists from the Eye of the Midnight Sun.

149
00:12:26,080 --> 00:12:28,080
Phew.

150
00:12:29,000 --> 00:12:32,200
So what do you want? Did you come here to get another beating from us?

151
00:12:33,040 --> 00:12:37,500
I noticed you're controlling a bunch of wraiths, so I'm guessing you're the one they call Radies.

152
00:12:38,760 --> 00:12:40,120
This guy gets it.

153
00:12:40,520 --> 00:12:42,040
We're on the hunt for something.

154
00:12:42,880 --> 00:12:43,660
Is that right?

155
00:12:44,420 --> 00:12:46,360
In this run-down old mess of a hideout?

156
00:12:46,840 --> 00:12:51,400
Ha! You may not know about it, but it's definitely here, and it's something good, too.

157
00:12:51,400 --> 00:12:55,200
Would you shut up?

158
00:12:55,540 --> 00:12:56,400
You idiots!

159
00:12:56,860 --> 00:13:01,260
Don't worry. We'll find it, and we might as well tear this place to pieces while we're at it!

160
00:13:01,360 --> 00:13:02,760
Ha ha ha ha ha ha ha ha ha!

161
00:13:02,820 --> 00:13:04,500
Not if I kill you first.

162
00:13:05,220 --> 00:13:07,640
Now, mirror magic, reflect ray!

163
00:13:07,700 --> 00:13:10,500
Cell magic, go Sticky Salamander!

164
00:13:11,840 --> 00:13:12,980
There it goes.

165
00:13:13,520 --> 00:13:17,120
I forgot. My kind of magic is useless against hers.

166
00:13:18,440 --> 00:13:19,980
There's no need to get upset.

167
00:13:19,980 --> 00:13:21,900
Goosh is your name, isn't it?

168
00:13:22,240 --> 00:13:27,360
You're not my target. In fact, I was specifically instructed to leave you alive, so you've got nothing to worry about!

169
00:13:27,740 --> 00:13:28,040
Huh?

170
00:13:28,500 --> 00:13:29,040
Oh, Q.

171
00:13:29,400 --> 00:13:30,440
What do you mean?

172
00:13:30,860 --> 00:13:34,160
To be honest, I'm not too sure. You'd have to ask Master Licht.

173
00:13:34,980 --> 00:13:36,680
Their leader really said that?

174
00:13:37,560 --> 00:13:38,720
Come to think of it.

175
00:13:39,340 --> 00:13:40,200
I'm sorry.

176
00:13:41,220 --> 00:13:42,980
I should never have...

177
00:13:43,520 --> 00:13:44,260
hurt you.

178
00:13:44,820 --> 00:13:45,100
Me?

179
00:13:45,400 --> 00:13:46,500
What are you talking about?

180
00:13:46,720 --> 00:13:49,280
Oh, didn't know you guys were friends or I wouldn't have beat him up.

181
00:13:49,280 --> 00:13:51,200
Of course I'm not friends with this monster.

182
00:13:51,700 --> 00:13:53,960
One day, you'll understand.

183
00:13:54,620 --> 00:13:56,080
Why did he say that?

184
00:13:56,400 --> 00:13:57,800
Come on, let's play!

185
00:13:58,500 --> 00:13:59,940
This might hurt a bit.

186
00:14:00,360 --> 00:14:02,960
So say your prayers, you black bulb-out heads!

187
00:14:02,960 --> 00:14:04,880
No time to ask questions.

188
00:14:04,880 --> 00:14:06,880
We've got to do something about these guys.

189
00:14:07,800 --> 00:14:11,000
The captain and the others probably won't be getting back for a while.

190
00:14:11,500 --> 00:14:13,340
Which means it's up to the three of us.

191
00:14:13,480 --> 00:14:14,320
Hmm, sure.

192
00:14:15,360 --> 00:14:15,840
Here!

193
00:14:16,800 --> 00:14:18,300
Dark magic item!

194
00:14:19,060 --> 00:14:20,180
Properties boost!

195
00:14:20,440 --> 00:14:21,560
Reinforce!

196
00:14:22,300 --> 00:14:25,060
Ta-da!

197
00:14:25,360 --> 00:14:26,320
You're all set!

198
00:14:26,460 --> 00:14:26,960
Let's go!

199
00:14:26,960 --> 00:14:27,960
Go!

200
00:14:34,760 --> 00:14:35,260
Go!

201
00:14:44,540 --> 00:14:46,120
Poison, curse, magic.

202
00:14:47,120 --> 00:14:48,580
I'll walk in the darks.

203
00:14:48,580 --> 00:15:01,300
Good work.

204
00:15:01,860 --> 00:15:02,660
Oh, Nate.

205
00:15:02,920 --> 00:15:04,800
That's some nasty poison you've got there.

206
00:15:05,040 --> 00:15:06,120
Doesn't matter, though.

207
00:15:07,080 --> 00:15:09,660
Because my shell could neutralize him easily!

208
00:15:09,660 --> 00:15:18,660
Mom, I should have told you, but...

209
00:15:18,660 --> 00:15:18,940
What?

210
00:15:19,200 --> 00:15:21,460
I actually learned a new spell that might be helpful!

211
00:15:22,540 --> 00:15:24,200
Uh, transformation magic!

212
00:15:24,540 --> 00:15:25,580
Magic compression!

213
00:15:28,580 --> 00:15:30,820
Changing gel magic into crystal magic?

214
00:15:31,020 --> 00:15:32,020
That's a surprise.

215
00:15:32,900 --> 00:15:33,840
There you go!

216
00:15:34,120 --> 00:15:35,020
Your turn, gosh!

217
00:15:35,480 --> 00:15:36,400
I see.

218
00:15:36,660 --> 00:15:39,520
Now I should be able to break it with mirror magic!

219
00:15:40,220 --> 00:15:41,340
Reflect refrain!

220
00:15:43,800 --> 00:15:45,140
Nice job!

221
00:15:48,180 --> 00:15:49,540
That was great!

222
00:15:49,700 --> 00:15:52,280
Your technique can change the very essence of a spell!

223
00:15:52,400 --> 00:15:53,880
You've really piqued my interest.

224
00:15:54,100 --> 00:15:56,800
I bet I could learn a lot by doing some experiments on you!

225
00:15:58,260 --> 00:15:59,220
Don't look at me!

226
00:15:59,280 --> 00:15:59,840
It was nothing!

227
00:16:02,100 --> 00:16:05,080
That'll just make it even more satisfying to crush you!

228
00:16:05,240 --> 00:16:05,900
Balthouse!

229
00:16:06,200 --> 00:16:06,640
Right.

230
00:16:06,640 --> 00:16:09,700
This guy's next!

231
00:16:10,160 --> 00:16:11,020
Number Zero!

232
00:16:11,780 --> 00:16:12,980
Mikael Caesar!

233
00:16:13,800 --> 00:16:15,040
What the hell?

234
00:16:15,800 --> 00:16:17,420
What's this creepy thing?

235
00:16:18,460 --> 00:16:19,540
You'll see!

236
00:16:19,540 --> 00:16:32,180
He can use two spells with different attributes at the same time?

237
00:16:32,460 --> 00:16:34,420
With such an incredible amount of force!

238
00:16:34,640 --> 00:16:37,560
Putting this big fella together really took a lot out of me!

239
00:16:38,020 --> 00:16:42,020
Yeah, but you never would have pulled it off without the help of my dark magic items, remember?

240
00:16:42,360 --> 00:16:43,700
Some things would be nice!

241
00:16:43,700 --> 00:16:45,960
He's made out of two different corpses!

242
00:16:46,420 --> 00:16:48,320
And that's not even the best part of it!

243
00:16:48,420 --> 00:16:50,560
Both of them were magic knight captains!

244
00:16:50,560 --> 00:17:14,120
Those cute little spells of yours may be clever parlor tricks!

245
00:17:14,120 --> 00:17:17,540
But they'll never be enough to defeat the perfect wraith I've created!

246
00:17:17,540 --> 00:17:24,920
This pathetic magic knight hideout is only getting in our way!

247
00:17:25,100 --> 00:17:27,360
Go ahead and decimate it for me!

248
00:17:30,000 --> 00:17:30,480
Attack!

249
